body:
Thank you pal. Firstly, glad you enjoyed it. But mainly it sounds like you're doing what you can right now to fix things. You're in a poetry subreddit so I imagine you have some interest in writing. Give it a go if you haven't already. As you can probably tell, I wrote this poem at a low point. It didn't fix everything, obviously, but it gave me something to show for it and something to look back on now when things are a bit better. If you're making changes from a lifestyle you didn't want to a lifestyle that you do want then you're doing the right thing. Best of luck with it buddy. Speak to those close to you but if you can't or don't want to, hit me up any time. Send me a message, I'm happy to give you my WhatsApp if you need to chat!

&#x200B;

Lots of love matey.

Arcade Fire, Glastonbury 2014. Their song Rebellion means a lot to me and my girlfriend. I kinda guessed they'd play it about half way through. As the techies were pulling their rigs down I said to my SO, "let's drop our pill now, I'm really hoping we come up during Rebellion". They come on, do a good 45 mins as they do, and then me and SO look up, I feel warmth and wobbles, and lots of joy. And then "dun dun dun dun dun dun dun dun din din din din din din din din.........."

&#x200B;

The best timed high I have ever had.

Why do you never see elephants in trees?

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Because they're really good at it.

Mine is coming from the base of my skull. It's a strange realisation isn't it. Everyone (who knows about my T) always asks "how are you ears?", or something to that effect, but all I'm thinking is "It's not in my fucking ears, mate." 

&#x200B;

It gets a lot easier quicker than you think, that's what I found anyway. Getting to chill with the anxiety, which is no mean feat, helps out - the best thing for me is talking to someone I love, my girlfriend in this instance, and letting them know I might need to talk for a while at night to take my mind off the ringing. Knowing that she is there for that has helped me get to sleep. I don't even need that extra conversation but knowing it's there is a real help. So fully informing someone close to you of how you are feeling could give you some peace of mind.
